 "text": "The clause is likely **not enforceable** as a mandatory term. Section 106 of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 prohibits a landlord from directly or indirectly requiring a tenant to pay rent by pre-authorized debit, or to provide post-dated cheques for rent. A tenant may agree to pay by pre-authorized debit voluntarily, but a clause that makes it a condition of the tenancy is unenforceable. Section 4 also voids any lease term that purports to waive or contract out of the Act's protections, so the clause would not be saved by the tenant's signature.\n\nI'm working from memory of the statute, so please confirm the exact wording of section 106 on e-Laws (ontario.ca/laws) before relying on it.\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 106",
